    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Gunnar Henderson** (70.51) serving as our primary engines. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** earns the top spot in our rankings against Houser, as the matchup provides a rare synergy of a favorable pitcher xERA and a significant platoon bump that elevates his production profile well above the daily baseline. Meanwhile, **Gunnar Henderson** remains a locked-in start despite facing the formidable Gilbert; the hitter-friendly park factors act as a massive hedge against the pitcher\u2019s skill, ensuring he remains a high-floor asset. Further, **Sam Antonacci** (62.91) continues to be an essential contributor, benefiting from a prime lead-off role against Holmes, making him a high-efficiency play for both R and SB categories.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's board involved **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (50.57), who narrowly missed the starting cut. While he remains a cornerstone of our offense, his efficiency was suppressed by a difficult matchup against Wheeler and a negative platoon split that dampened his baseline projection. He was ultimately edged out by the superior matchup context for **Nolan Schanuel** (50.89), whose favorable spot in the order against the weaker arm of Teng provided a more reliable path to point accumulation. We must also exercise caution regarding the bottom of our outfield depth: both **Kyle Tucker** (50.54) and **Andy Pages** (46.24) are facing Skenes, an elite arm capable of neutralizing even the most talented bats. While we are starting them to maintain our category coverage, the significant SP Skill penalty applied to their scores is a stark reminder that their value rests on their ability to beat a high-strikeout pitcher rather than an exploitable matchup.",
